          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong double category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal category
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            %strong double groupoid
            is an internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
          %p
            However, these definitions obscure the essential symmetry of the concepts. We think of a double category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1 \stackrel{\to}{\to} D_0
            as having
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              \: the objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+morphisms"} vertical morphisms
              \: the morphisms of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_0
            %li
              %em>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+morphisms"} horizontal morphisms
              \: the objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphisms"} 2-morphisms
              or
              %em squares
              or
              = succeed ":" do
                %em 2-cells
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi D
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_1
          %p We may picture a 2-cell in a double category as a square:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi α
                                  %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ⇓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ϕ
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi α
                                  %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi y
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{matrix}
                  x_0
                  \&amp;\stackrel{f}{\to} &amp;
                  x_1
                  \\\
                  {}^{\mathllap{\alpha_0}}\downarrow
                  \&amp;\Downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi}}&amp;
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\alpha_1}}
                  \\\
                  y_0
                  \&amp;\underset{g}{\to} &amp;
                  y_1
                  \\end{matrix}
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i,y_i
            are objects,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            are horizontal arrows,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_i
            are vertical arrows and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            is the 2-cell itself. This makes it clear why
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            is called a ‘square’.
          %p
            Alternatively one can apply
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré duality
            to obtain a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            representation for 2-cells, similar to the one obtained for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#Myers16"}> Myers 16
            ):
