          %h3#references References
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Böhm20"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriella+B%C3%B6hm"}> Gabriella Böhm
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Gray monoidal product of double categories
            %li#Campbell19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Campbell"}> Alexander Campbell
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em How strict is strictification?
          %p An exploration of the possibility of a closed structure on strict double categories and lax functors may be found in:
          %ul
            %li
              %span.newWikiWord>
                Bojana Femić
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Bojana+Femi%C4%87"} ?
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bifunctor Theorem and strictification tensor product for double categories with lax double functors
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.13452"} arXiv:2207.13452
              (2022).
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew+monoidal+category"} Skew monoidal
            structures are constructed on categories of double categories in:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Femić24"}
              %span.newWikiWord>
                Bojana Femić
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Bojana+Femi%C4%87"} ?
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Gray (skew) multicategories: double and Gray-categorical cases
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.00561"} arXiv:2408.00561
              (2024).
          %h2#model_structures_on_the_category_of_double_categories Model structures on the category of double categories
          %p
            The category of strict double categories admits a plethora of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} Quillen model structures
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FPPModel"} Fiore, Paoli, and Pronk
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FPThomason"} Fiore and Paoli
            %a{:href => "#MSV2Cat"} Moser, Sarazola, and Verdugo I
            and
            %a{:href => "#MSVHInvar"} Moser, Sarazola, and Verdugo II
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CampbellGreg"} Campbell
          %p
            For more see
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+DblCat"} model structure on DblCat
          %h3#gregarious_model_structure Gregarious model structure
          %p
            The
            %strong gregarious model structure
            on the category of double categories is defined uniquely by the following two properties:
          %ul
            %li Every double category is fibrant.
            %li A double functor is a trivial fibration if it is surjective on objects, full on horizontal morphisms, full on vertical morphisms, and fully faithful on double cells.
          %p
            Weak equivalences in this model structure can be characterized as follows. A double functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon A\to B
            is a weak equivalence in the gregarious model structure for double categories if and only if it satisfies the following four conditions.
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is surjective on objects up to gregarious equivalence, meaning that for every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b\in B
              there is an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
              and a gregarious equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fa
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fa\to b
              in
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is full on horizontal morphisms up to globular isomorphism;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is full on vertical morphisms up to globular isomorphism;
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is fully faithful on double cells.
          %p
            Here a
            %em globular isomorphism
            is an invertible 2-cell in the horizontal respectively vertical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            associated to the given double category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            A
            %strong gregarious equivalence
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/companion+pair"} companion pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f,u)
            of morphisms in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is an equivalence in the horizontal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi u
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
            is an equivalence in the vertical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+equipped+with+proarrows"}> 2-category equipped with proarrows
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+bicategory"} framed bicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+double+category"} virtual double category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+functor"}> double functor
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+pseudofunctor"} double pseudofunctor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+transformation"}> vertical transformation
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+transformation"} horizontal transformation
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+profunctor"} double profunctor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+limit"} double limit
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+double+category"}> monoidal double category
                ,
                %span.newWikiWord
                  locally double bicategory
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/locally+double+bicategory"} ?
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triple+category"}> triple category
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intercategory"} intercategory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiple+category"} multiple category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/applications+of+double+category+theory"} applications of double category theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right-connected+double+category"} right-connected double category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+fibration"} double fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+infinity-category"} double infinity-category
          %h2#references_2 References
          %p The concept goes back to:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories double et catégories structurées
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Ehresmann-CategoriesDoubles.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k3208j/f1246"} gallica
            %li#Ehresmann63
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
                , Déf. 10, p. 389 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Catégories structurées
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/urn:eudml:doc:81794"} eudml:81794
          %p For a comprehensive treatment, it is probably best to consult the series of papers by Grandis and Paré:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Marco Grandis and Robert Paré,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/article/CTGDC_1999__40_3_162_0.pdf"} Limits in double categories
                %em Cahiers de Topologie et Géométrie Différentielle Catégoriques
                %strong 40
                (1999), 162–220.
            %li
              %p
                Marco Grandis and Robert Paré,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/article/CTGDC_2004__45_3_193_0.pdf"} Adjoints for double categories
                %em Cahiers de Topologie et Géométrie Différentielle Catégoriques
                %strong 45
                (2004), 193–240.
            %li
              %p
                Marco Grandis and Robert Paré,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/20/8/20-08abs.html"} Kan extensions in double categories (On weak double categories, Part III)
            %li
              %p
                Marco Grandis and Robert Paré,
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/article/CTGDC_2007__48_3_163_0.pdf"} Lax Kan extensions for double categories (On weak double categories, Part IV)
                Cahiers de topologie et géométrie différentielle catégoriques, tome 48, no 3 (2007), p. 163-199
          %p For basic theory of the (virtual) double category of presheaves on a double category, the Yoneda embedding, and the density theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Robert Paré
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/25/17/25-17abs.html"} Yoneda theory for double categories
            %li
              %p
                Robert Paré
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/27/16/27-16abs.html"} Composition of Modules for Lax Functors
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#JohnsonYau20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niles+Johnson"}> Niles Johnson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"} Donald Yau
                = succeed "," do
                  %em 2-Dimensional Categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/2002.06055"} arXiv:2002.06055
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://oxford.universitypressscholarship.com/view/10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001/oso-9780198871378"} doi:10.1093/oso/9780198871378.001.0001
            %li#Grandis19
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher dimensional categories: from double to multiple categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/11406"} doi:10.1142/11406
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Catsters"}> The Catsters
                , Double Categories (
                %a{:href => "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kiCZiSA2W3Q&feature=channel_page"}> YouTube
                ).
            %li
              %p
                Tom Fiore,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www-personal.umd.umich.edu/~tmfiore/1/CT2006Fioreslides.pdf"} Double categories and pseudo algebras
            %li
              %p
                Jeffrey C. Morton,
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611930"} Double bicategories and double cospans
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
                and C.B. Spencer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/CTGDC_1976__17_4_343_0"} Double groupoids and crossed modules
                %em Cahiers de Topologie et Géométrie Différentielle Catégoriques
                %strong 17
                (1976), 343–362.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronnie+Brown"} Ronnie Brown
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Higgins"} Philip Higgins
                %a{:href => "http://archive.numdam.org/ARCHIVE/CTGDC/CTGDC_1981__22_4/CTGDC_1981__22_4_371_0/CTGDC_1981__22_4_371_0.pdf"}
                  The equivalence of
                  = succeed "-groupoids" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed "." do
                  %em Cah. Top. Géom. Diff
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://nyjm.albany.edu/j/2011/17-5v.pdf"} Comparing composites of left and right derived functors
                %em New York J. Math.
                %strong 17
                (2011) 75–125.
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.2868"} arXiv:0706.2868
            %li#Myers16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Jaz+Myers"}> David Jaz Myers
                ,
                %em String diagrams for double categories and (virtual) equipments
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1612.02762"}> arXiv:1612.02762
                )
            %li
              %p
                Kenny Courser,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Open systems: a double categorical perspective
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.02394"} arxiv/2008.02394
            %li
              %p
                Antonin Delpeuch,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The word problem for double categories
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.09927"} arxiv
            %li
              %p
                Virtual Double Categories Workshop, 2022 (
                %a{:href => "https://bryceclarke.github.io/virtual-double-categories-workshop/2022/index.html"}> webpage
                )
            %li
              %p
                Second Virtual Workshop on Double Categories, 2024 (
                %a{:href => "https://bryceclarke.github.io/virtual-double-categories-workshop/index.html"}> webpage
                )
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures+on+DblCat"} model structures on DblCat
          %ul
            %li#FPPModel
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+M.+Fiore"}> Thomas M. Fiore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simona+Paoli"} Simona Paoli
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dorette+A.+Pronk"} Dorette A. Pronk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Model structures on the category of small double categories
                %em Algebraic &amp; Geometric Topology
                %strong 8
                (2008) 1855–1959 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2008.8.1855"}> doi:10.2140/agt.2008.8.1855
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#FPThomason
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Fiore"}> Thomas Fiore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simona+Paoli"} Simona Paoli
                %em
                  A Thomason model structure on the category of small
                  = succeed "-fold" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %em Algebraic &amp; Geometric Topology
                %strong 10
                (2010) 1933–2008 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://doi.org/10.2140/agt.2010.10.1933"}> doi:10.2140/agt.2010.10.1933
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#MSV2Cat
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lyne+Moser"}> Lyne Moser
                , Maru Sarazola, Paula Verdugo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    A
                    = succeed "-inspired" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mi Cat
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2Cat
                = succeed "2" do
                  %strong LXIII
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.14233"} arxiv:2004.14233
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://cahierstgdc.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/MoserSarazolaVerdugo-LXIII-2.pdf"} pdf
            %li#CampbellGreg
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Campbell"}> Alexander Campbell
                ,
                %em The gregarious model structure for double categories
                (2020) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://acmbl.github.io/greg_slides.pdf"}> talk slides pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#MSVHInvar
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lyne+Moser"}> Lyne Moser
                , Maru Sarazola, Paula Verdugo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A model structure for weakly horizontally invariant double categories
                %strong 23
                4 (2023) 1725-1786 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.00588"}> arxiv:2007.00588
                , journal:
                %a{:href => "https://msp.org/agt/2023/23-4/agt-v23-n4-p08-p.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            For the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"}> bicategorically
            ) cartesian closed structure, see:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Double clubs
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0606733"} arXiv
          %p
            An explicit description of what it means to be a one-object double category (i.e. filling in the gap in “a delooping of a ___ is a double category”) is given in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/3790232"} this Math.StackExchange answer
          %p
            For
            %span.newWikiWord
              univalent double categories
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/univalent+double+categories"} ?
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+van+der+Weide"}> Niels van der Weide
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nima+Rasekh"} Nima Rasekh
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benedikt+Ahrens"} Benedikt Ahrens
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paige+Randall+North"} Paige Randall North
              %em Univalent Double Categories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.09220"}> arXiv:2310.09220
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+category+theory"} formal category theory
            within double categories:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seerp+Roald+Koudenburg"}> Seerp Roald Koudenburg
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formal category theory in augmented virtual double categories
                %strong 41
                10 (2024) 288–413 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.04890"}> arXiv:2205.04890
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.70930/tac/dc4prz63"} doi:10.70930/tac/dc4prz63
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seerp+Roald+Koudenburg"}> Seerp Roald Koudenburg
                \:
                %em A double-dimensional approach to formal category theory
                (2015–) &amp;lbrack;
